From 0bab7247888fd441318d02ca08e59a5d465a77fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Sanchez <juanesf91@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:56:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 41/43] arm64: dts: allwinner: cubie-a7a: disable EEE on the
 Maxio PHY

The Cubie A7A uses a Maxio MAE0621A-Q3C PHY (ID 0x7b744412), for which
mainline has no dedicated driver, so the generic PHY driver binds. With
EEE advertised the 1Gbps link drops and re-negotiates every few minutes
(~4 s down, phy_eee_wakeup_error_n incrementing) and NetworkManager
restarts DHCP on each flap. The vendor MAXIO driver disables both EEE
modes; the linux-sunxi discussion of this exact PHY confirmed this is the
known A7A problem ("they disable the two EEE modes that you got problems
with on the A7A, in the PHY driver").

Use the standard DT flags parsed by phy-core (of_set_phy_eee_broken) so
the two 100/1000BASE-T EEE modes are no longer advertised. This is the
mainline equivalent of the vendor workaround and needs no new driver.
The MAC-side RGMII delays stay untouched: the link is error-free
(0 CRC / 0 align / 0 FIFO overflow) at 1000 Mb/s Full.

Signed-off-by: Juan Sanchez <juanesf91@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7a.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7a.dts
index ffcc030b5..e242ca560 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7a.dts
@@ -187,6 +187,14 @@ ext_rgmii_phy: ethernet-phy@1 {
 			reset-gpios = <&pio 7 16 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>; /* PH16 */
 			reset-assert-us = <10000>;
 			reset-deassert-us = <150000>;
+			/*
+			 * MAE0621A-Q3C: the vendor PHY driver disables both
+			 * EEE modes. With the generic PHY driver, leaving EEE
+			 * advertised makes the link drop and re-negotiate
+			 * every few minutes (phy_eee_wakeup_error_n).
+			 */
+			eee-broken-100tx;
+			eee-broken-1000t;
 		};
 	};
 };
